{
  "source_lines": [
    {
      "line_index": 0,
      "text": "When comparing the features between Group 2 and Group 3, the results revealed statistically significant differences in the",
      "physical_page": 6,
      "assigned": true
    },
    {
      "line_index": 1,
      "text": "signs of bronchial inflation sign (P < 0.001), vascular convergence sign (P = 0.010), lobulation sign (P < 0.001), pleural trac-",
      "physical_page": 6,
      "assigned": true
    },
    {
      "line_index": 2,
      "text": "tion sign (P = 0.003), CTR > 0.5 (P < 0.001), and the diameter of nodule (P < 0.001) between the two groups. These features",
      "physical_page": 6,
      "assigned": true
    },
    {
      "line_index": 3,
      "text": "were included in the binary logistic regression, and ultimately, CTR > 0.5 and the diameter of nodule were identified as",
      "physical_page": 6,
      "assigned": true
    },
    {
      "line_index": 4,
      "text": "independent risk factors for underestimating IAC patients. CTR ≤ 0.5 and smaller nodule diameter are associated with the",
      "physical_page": 6,
      "assigned": true
    },
    {
      "line_index": 5,
      "text": "underestimation of IAC in FS. The AUC for the diameter of nodule was 0.681, with a cut-off value of 12.55 mm. (Table 4).",
      "physical_page": 6,
      "assigned": true
    },
    {
      "line_index": 6,
      "text": "Table 4 Univariate and",
      "physical_page": 7,
      "assigned": true
    },
    {
      "line_index": 7,
      "text": "multivariate analysis between",
      "physical_page": 7,
      "assigned": true
    },
    {
      "line_index": 8,
      "text": "group 2 and group 3",
      "physical_page": 7,
      "assigned": true
    },
    {
      "line_index": 9,
      "text": "12.70 (± 4.69) 16.19 (± 5.79) < 0.001* < 0.001* 0.888",
      "physical_page": 7,
      "assigned": true
    }
  ],
